                "place_type": null,
                "poll": null,
                "post_type": "post",
                "quote_count": 100,
                "quoted_status_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 299,
                "retweet_count": 1348,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "During 2022 and 2023, Pharma and healthcare companies paid NIAID $690 million in royalties. Besides Pfizer, Merck, and Moderna (which paid a separate $400 million) two of the top pharma companies paying NIAID were owned by the Chinese government.\n\nIn prior years, NIAID received about $2 million per year in royalties. COVID produced a massive haul for Fauci\u2019s agency. But the names of many at the agency who received the money remain redacted. Even getting this much information required two FOIA lawsuits filed by Open the Books and Judicial Watch.\n\nAmerica\u2019s public health agencies are corrupt. How can we trust them when they profit from the products they promote (and mandate)?\n\nAs President, I will clean up the corruption in Washington, and flip the program to bring back real health care. #KennedyShanahan24",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1717862435,
