                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 739,
                "retweet_count": 1404,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "$4 milk, $4 bread, and car insurance premiums are up 22% in a year.\n\n70% of Americans earn less than the cost of basic needs.\n\nHousing is now so expensive that anyone who has a house is staying put because a new mortgage has a vastly higher rate than the old one. They'd have to pay far more for the same size house. It\u2019s musical chairs. All the people lucky enough to have a house before the music stopped aren\u2019t budging and everyone else is outta luck. Nobody being able to move means a scarcity of homes on the market, which drives prices higher, and the vicious cycle continues.\n\nAll of this is the predictable result of rate hikes to fight inflation caused by printing money for President Trump\u2019s corporate tax cuts, Presidents Trump and Biden\u2019s lockdowns, and President Biden\u2019s Ukraine war. Now Biden is printing more money to buy votes with another round of student debt forgiveness and people wonder why rates are staying high\u2026",
